WEBVTT

00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:02.731
Your agent's model affects how it reasons how

00:00:02.751 --> 00:00:05.422
quickly it responds and how many AI Credits

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:07.803
it uses In this guide we'll choose a

00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:10.755
model in Hatcher understand the default and compare

00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:12.946
the cost of everyday work with more demanding

00:00:12.966 --> 00:00:13.621
tasks

00:00:14.756 --> 00:00:17.879
First separate three things The framework such as

00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:20.808
OpenClaw or Hermes runs the agent and its

00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:24.542
tools The language model handles reasoning and responses

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:27.403
The provider route delivers that model Changing the

00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:30.828
model does not automatically add skills grant permissions

00:00:31.006 --> 00:00:32.233
or change your hosting plan

00:00:33.354 --> 00:00:35.786
When creating an agent describe its job and

00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:38.989
review the generated preview Find AI route then

00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:41.810
Hosted model Choose a provider family pick a

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.739
model and review its context and cost information

00:00:44.759 --> 00:00:47.500
before hatching The suggested setup is a starting

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.417
point make sure it fits the work you

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:50.378
actually want done

00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:54.277
For an existing agent open its workspace go

00:00:54.297 --> 00:00:57.503
to Config and select Model and Provider Keep

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.955
Managed by Hatcher to use hosted models and

00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:04.015
AI Credits Use the search provider filters capability

00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:06.642
tags and cost range to narrow the list

00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:09.920
Check the model description context window and current

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:10.440
pricing

00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:13.950
Selecting a model changes the draft It does

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.534
not save the agent yet Compare Saved model

00:01:16.554 --> 00:01:19.685
with Draft selection then click Save AI Models

00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.864
Wait for the confirmation and any runtime restart

00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:25.117
Check the active model in chat before your

00:01:25.137 --> 00:01:28.542
next task Saved presets help you reuse choices

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:30.983
but still require saving the configuration

00:01:32.099 --> 00:01:35.397
The current Hatcher catalog marks DeepSeek V4 Flash

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.043
as the default hosted model It is positioned

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:41.103
as a fast economical starting point Your agent

00:01:41.123 --> 00:01:43.424
may already have a different saved or suggested

00:01:43.444 --> 00:01:46.091
model so check it Default does not mean

00:01:46.111 --> 00:01:48.290
the strongest model and it does not mean

00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:50.686
automatic selection of the best model for every

00:01:50.706 --> 00:01:51.254
task

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:56.155
For summaries extraction simple replies and repeated routine

00:01:56.175 --> 00:01:59.449
work start by evaluating economical options such as

00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:03.274
DeepSeek V4 Flash or Gemini Flash Lite GPT

00:02:03.294 --> 00:02:06.342
mini models are candidates for broader everyday work

00:02:06.675 --> 00:02:09.774
DeepSeek Pro offers another step toward more demanding

00:02:09.794 --> 00:02:12.822
analysis These are starting points for testing not

00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:14.247
a universal quality ranking

00:02:15.378 --> 00:02:19.096
For difficult coding planning or long instructions compare

00:02:19.116 --> 00:02:22.152
stronger options such as Claude Sonnet Claude Opus

00:02:22.354 --> 00:02:26.390
GPT's higher capability variants or Gemini Pro Codex

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:29.131
and Qwen coding models are also worth evaluating

00:02:29.151 --> 00:02:31.893
for repository work A more capable model may

00:02:31.913 --> 00:02:34.441
follow constraints better but can cost more and

00:02:34.461 --> 00:02:36.771
take longer Always review the result

00:02:37.899 --> 00:02:40.495
The catalog also includes families such as MiMo

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.415
MiniMax Kimi GLM Grok Mistral and SERV Compare

00:02:45.435 --> 00:02:48.415
their individual descriptions and prices A provider name

00:02:48.435 --> 00:02:50.780
alone does not tell you quality or cost

00:02:51.101 --> 00:02:53.605
A large context window means more room for

00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:57.236
information not guaranteed accuracy Partner routes can have

00:02:57.256 --> 00:02:59.209
different pricing and data policies

00:03:00.309 --> 00:03:03.848
AI Credits meter hosted usage Language models process

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:07.416
tokens chunks of text Input includes your prompt

00:03:07.594 --> 00:03:10.527
instructions history and tool results sent to the

00:03:10.547 --> 00:03:14.523
model Output includes generated tokens and where billed

00:03:14.773 --> 00:03:19.003
reasoning tokens Longer conversations larger files and repeated

00:03:19.023 --> 00:03:21.908
tool loops can increase usage One user message

00:03:21.928 --> 00:03:23.583
can trigger several model calls

00:03:24.675 --> 00:03:27.465
Hatcher's billing reference is one thousand AI Credits

00:03:27.485 --> 00:03:30.262
per dollar of provider usage Credit pack checkout

00:03:30.282 --> 00:03:33.143
prices are separate Read both input and output

00:03:33.163 --> 00:03:36.810
rates usually shown per million tokens Actual charges

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:40.048
use reported provider cost when available otherwise an

00:03:40.068 --> 00:03:43.084
estimate applies Positive model charges round up to

00:03:43.104 --> 00:03:45.521
whole credits with a one credit minimum

00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:49.027
Here is an illustrative single call using ten

00:03:49.047 --> 00:03:52.238
thousand input tokens and two thousand output tokens

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:56.086
Using the catalog snapshot DeepSeek V4 Flash works

00:03:56.106 --> 00:03:58.872
out to about one credit after rounding GPT

00:03:58.892 --> 00:04:01.717
five point four mini is about seventeen Claude

00:04:01.737 --> 00:04:04.372
Sonnet four point six is about sixty These

00:04:04.392 --> 00:04:07.396
are list based estimates not recorded charges or

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:08.511
a quality benchmark

00:04:09.642 --> 00:04:11.726
A cheaper call can become expensive if the

00:04:11.773 --> 00:04:14.920
agent repeats itself or needs several corrections A

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.761
stronger model can sometimes finish in fewer steps

00:04:17.951 --> 00:04:20.634
but savings are not guaranteed Compare the same

00:04:20.654 --> 00:04:25.583
task instructions tools and output requirements Check correctness

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:29.634
completion time and total credits including retries Keep

00:04:29.654 --> 00:04:31.654
the option that meets your quality target

00:04:32.754 --> 00:04:36.127
Hosted search research embeddings and media tools can

00:04:36.147 --> 00:04:38.270
add their own charges With Use your own

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.758
provider supported model calls are billed to your

00:04:40.778 --> 00:04:44.139
provider account instead of Hatcher AI Credits Hosted

00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:46.984
tools may still use credits Review your remaining

00:04:47.004 --> 00:04:50.317
balance and usage history in Billing an estimate

00:04:50.337 --> 00:04:53.210
or temporary reservation is not necessarily the final

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:53.754
charge

00:04:54.875 --> 00:04:57.153
Start with an economical model for a small

00:04:57.173 --> 00:05:00.581
representative task If it misses requirements improve the

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:03.629
instructions and test a stronger model Use focused

00:05:03.649 --> 00:05:06.320
context and a clear output length Save your

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.864
preferred configuration then monitor usage as work grows

00:05:10.197 --> 00:05:11.689
You are choosing the right model for a

00:05:11.709 --> 00:05:14.495
job not buying a guarantee of better answers

00:05:15.609 --> 00:05:18.600
Open your agent choose Model and Provider review

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.410
the current prices and save your selection Start

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.684
with a sensible default Spend more when the

00:05:23.704 --> 00:05:26.017
task earns it Build and manage your agents

00:05:26.037 --> 00:05:27.180
at Hatcher dot host